-- A thumbnail belongs to a resolved appearance, not to a saved variant, a
-- label or an armor record: the same look reached from two variants is one
-- image, and an edited variant simply asks for another key. The key is the
-- slot, the body, the piece, the pack's content hash and the look's toggle
-- word, under a renderer version that changes when the capture does.
--
-- Images are 240 x 240 RGBA cells, 25 to a 1200 x 1200 page file
-- (`preview-page-<n>.rgba`, raw, row 0 at the top). The manifest
-- (`preview-cache.state`) names each key's page and cell with a checksum of
-- its pixels; a cell whose pixels no longer match is forgotten, never shown.
-- A tile (the Armory page draws its three gear tiles several times the size
-- of a card) is one image at the capture's own side, in a file of its own
-- (`preview-tile-<n>-<side>.rgba`), named in the manifest the same way.
--
-- files.read(name) -> string|nil; files.write(name, text) -> true|nil, why
-- (atomic); files.patch(name, size, writes) -> true|nil, why creates a zeroed
-- file of `size` bytes when absent and writes each {offset=, bytes=}.
local M={}
M.RENDERER='p6'   -- pristine visual templates; discard images composed from mutated sources
M.DEFAULT_STYLE='rim'
M.STYLES={rim='rim-v1',studio='studio-v1',classic='classic-v1'}
M.CELL=240;M.COLUMNS=5;M.PER_PAGE=25;M.PAGE=1200
M.CELL_BYTES=M.CELL*M.CELL*4;M.PAGE_BYTES=M.PAGE*M.PAGE*4
M.MAX_ENTRIES=4000
M.MAX_TILE=4096
M.MANIFEST='preview-cache.state'
